  "lessons": [
    {
      "title": "Hello, {First}! Welcome to the Top Down Raglan Course",
      "slug": "hello-first-welcome-to-the-top-down-raglan-course",
      "displayOrder": 1,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 35,
        "lessonOrder": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<div class=\"lead\">Welcome, {First}!</div>\r\nTop down raglan sweaters are long-time favorites for machine knitters.  The raglan shaping is flattering on everyone and the unusual construction can provide a challenge from traditional \"knit-in-pieces\" sweaters.<br>\r\nWe can play with yarn and stitch patterns. They offer an opportunity for us to gain confidence in our knitting.\r\n<blockquote class=\"smallblock\">\r\nWhen knitting top down sweaters,  little planning can go a long way!\r\n<ul class=”Instruction-list”>\r\n<li>Have you ever started a project unsure if you have enough yarn?</li>\r\n<li>Why guess at how many stitches to cast on?</li>\r\n<li>Want to create something that you will be proud of... good enough to enter in the fair?</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</blockquote>\r\nThis course will walk you through all the planning steps and show you step by step the knitting in progress. <br> It shows techniques that may be new to you and helps you record your progress.<br>If this is your first sweater or your tenth, follow along, the skills you gain here will be invaluable for future knitting projects .. not just this style of sweater!\r\n<blockquote class=\"smallblock\">\r\nIf you are new here, the next video will help you learn to navigate this course so you can get the most benefit from the material that is included. It will walk you through how to access the lessons and navigate to get the most out of your course.<br />\r\n</blockquote>",
              "legacyComponentId": 451,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<b>Don't skip lessons ... you may feel that you know how to work a technique ... but sometimes you will pick up a tip that you can use while watching a video.</b><br>",
              "legacyComponentId": 490,
              "order": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "221120492",
              "title": "Machine Knitting Courses",
              "legacyComponentId": 491,
              "order": 4
            }
          ],
          "title": "START HERE",
          "slug": "start-here",
          "order": 1,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 159,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Lesson 1: Plan your project",
      "slug": "lesson-1-plan-your-project",
      "displayOrder": 2,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 36,
        "lessonOrder": 2
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "For success in machine knitting, using the appropriate yarn for your machine is critical.<br>Also consider the care of the finished sweater.  You may be looking to make an heirloom sweater and want to use an exquisite natural fiber.  More than likely, you want to knit a hard wearing, easy care sweater. Consider the recipient when you make your yarn choice.<br><blockquote class=\"smallblock\"><b>TIP:</b><br><em>If your sweater will be a gift, you may want to include a note with the fiber content of the yarn used and suggested care instructions.</em></blockquote>",
              "legacyComponentId": 453,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "migrationPending",
              "legacyType": "DataEntry",
              "notes": [
                "Unmapped legacy component type: DataEntry"
              ],
              "legacyFields": {
